 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ENVOK.
 AUTHOR. A STUDENT.
 DATE-WRITTEN. 12 NOV 2026.
 REMARKS. READS DATA FROM A FILE, 3 TIMES.
* everything here is taken: free text with numbers
* and DATA in it, the CONFIGURATION SECTION, FD
* clauses with a count, SELECT OPTIONAL, key and
* status names over ten characters, VALUES ARE,
* OCCURS ... TIMES, USAGE IS COMP-3, SIGN SEPARATE
*   E1 00 / E2 00 / E3 ABCD 00 / E4 Y / E5 2 -005
 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
 SOURCE-COMPUTER. APPLE-IIE.
 OBJECT-COMPUTER. APPLE-IIE.
 SPECIAL-NAMES.
     INPUT CASE IS UPPERCASE ONLY.
 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
 FILE-CONTROL.
     SELECT OPTIONAL ENV-FILE ASSIGN TO "ENVOK.DAT"
         ORGANIZATION IS RELATIVE
         ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
         RELATIVE KEY IS THE-RELATIVE-KEY-ITEM
         FILE STATUS IS THE-FILE-STATUS-ITEM.
 DATA DIVISION.
 FILE SECTION.
 FD  ENV-FILE
     LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
     RECORD CONTAINS 12 CHARACTERS.
 01  ENV-REC.
     05  ER-NAME  PIC X(4).
     05  ER-AMT   PIC S9(5)V99 USAGE IS COMP-3.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 77  THE-RELATIVE-KEY-ITEM PIC 9(4) COMP.
 77  THE-FILE-STATUS-ITEM  PIC XX.
 01  T-TAB.
     05  T-ENT PIC 9 OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 01  W-FLAG PIC X VALUE "B".
     88  W-B VALUES ARE "B".
 01  W-SIGN PIC S9(3) SIGN IS LEADING SEPARATE
         CHARACTER VALUE -5.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
 MAIN-PARA.
     OPEN OUTPUT ENV-FILE.
     DISPLAY "E1 " THE-FILE-STATUS-ITEM.
     MOVE 1 TO THE-RELATIVE-KEY-ITEM.
     MOVE "ABCD" TO ER-NAME.
     MOVE 12.5 TO ER-AMT.
     WRITE ENV-REC.
     DISPLAY "E2 " THE-FILE-STATUS-ITEM.
     CLOSE ENV-FILE.
     OPEN I-O ENV-FILE.
     MOVE SPACES TO ER-NAME.
     READ ENV-FILE INVALID KEY DISPLAY "E3 BAD".
     DISPLAY "E3 " ER-NAME " " THE-FILE-STATUS-ITEM.
     CLOSE ENV-FILE.
     IF W-B DISPLAY "E4 Y" ELSE DISPLAY "E4 N".
     MOVE 2 TO T-ENT(2).
     DISPLAY "E5 " T-ENT(2) " " W-SIGN.
     STOP RUN.
